### Explanation:
- \( D_p \): Diameter at point p.
- \( D_m \): Diameter at midpoint.
- \( (RPM)_m \): Revolutions per minute at midpoint.
- \( (RPM)_p \): Revolutions per minute at point p.

These formulas relate the diameters and revolutions per minute at different points on a rotating object, likely a gear or a similar mechanical component.
